                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_25\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit adds a single line, `filesFromThisSite.clear();`, at the start of\nXMLFileReader.read(), right after `this.updateSite = updateSite;`. The commit\nmessage says the bug \"would prevent any shadowing (update sites overriding\nother update sites' files)\".\n\nThe `filesFromThisSite` field was introduced in candidate_25. In that commit,\nthe field is declared and initialized once as an instance field:\n\n    protected Set<FileObject> filesFromThisSite = new HashSet<FileObject>();\n\nThe read() logic in that same commit was reworked so that, instead of\ncomparing `updateSite` strings to decide whether an existing FileObject came\nfrom the same update site as the one currently being parsed, it checks\n`filesFromThisSite.contains(file)`. This set is populated with every\nFileObject added while processing the current call to read(), but it is never\ncleared when read() is called again for a different update site (read() is\ncalled once per update site while building the merged file list). As a\nresult, files added while parsing one update site remain in\n`filesFromThisSite` when a later update site is parsed, so the code\nincorrectly treats files from a previous update site as if they belonged to\nthe site currently being read. This causes the shadowing/override logic\n(`filesFromThisSite.contains(file)` branch vs. the `getRank(...)` branch that\nhandles the overridden-update-site bookkeping and the \"shadows\" warning) to\ntake the wrong path, effectively preventing update sites from overriding each\nother's files \u2014 precisely the symptom described in the fix commit message.\n\nCandidate_26 (a later change) only refactors the warning output (using\n`files.log.warn` instead of appending to `warnings`) and does not touch the\nmissing-clear() issue, so it does not fix or reintroduce the bug \u2014 it simply\ncarries it forward. The very next change to this method is the fix commit\nitself, which adds `filesFromThisSite.clear()`. Since candidate_25 is the\ncommit that first introduced the `filesFromThisSite` field and the logic that\ndepends on it being properly reset per update site (but omitted that reset),\nit is the bug-introducing commit.\n"
                }
              }
